From 8148e56fa72a22cf4d7173891223d9550920d69d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a per-attempt re-mark button for admins
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The only existing re-mark tool (POST /api/admin/results/remark) re-marks an
entire account's worth of completed attempts at once — the right tool for
"re-mark everybody after a scoring change", but overkill and imprecise for
"did this one code change actually move this one attempt's marks", which is
what checking a fix in place actually calls for.

- routes/admin.js: POST /api/admin/results/:id/remark re-marks a single
  attempt (same markAttempt/retranscribeAndMark path as the batch route,
  same REMARKABLE status guard), awaited directly since one attempt is a
  short enough wait to hold the request open for.
- public/app.js: a "Re-mark this attempt" button next to the existing
  admin-only band-correction panel on the result screen. Reports the
  before/after score and level so the admin can see at a glance whether
  anything moved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LgKXYQSxMY9AyY5uyuhSbh
